window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>It's hard being a beta</b> <b>boxer in an alpha world, especially when you have so much to lose.</b></p> <p>As a female boxer, and a beta to boot, I've had to dig deep for every win, train harder than every opponent, and ignore the naysayers along the way.</p> <p>I'm just starting to make my mark when I lose an easy match, and my manager says I need to overhaul my image. Sponsors are losing interest, and I'm struggling to keep my dad's gym afloat. I'll do anything to keep his dream alive, even attend the grand opening of a new sports club so people can rub shoulders with a professional boxer.</p> <p>But that night changes a lot of things. Not only do I find out my ex—a famous polo-playing billionaire—owns the club, but the international rugby team is in town. My bruised and battered face fires up their protective alpha instincts, and I'm suddenly triggered by a switch.</p> <p>Even though I pride myself on my control, my hidden omega nature takes over, hungry for knots, bites, and a pack of my own.</p> <p>I always thought switches were a beta fantasy. But now I have three alphas, a beta best friend, and a stunning omega male all vying to see me through my heat. Maybe it's a fairytale for some girls, but this changes everything.</p> <p>Because while being a beta boxer was hard, the world will never accept an omega in the ring. Which means I have to choose. But do I fight for the pack who wants me, or for the win I always wanted for myself?</p> <p><i>This is the fourth steamy standalone in the Billionaires in Heat series but can be enjoyed as a standalone. It includes all the omegaverse delights of pack bonds, bites, messy heats, and alpha knots. There are no shifters in this story. For mature listeners.</i></p>"; 
